# Atlas environment template (PRD §21 Q24, decided 2026-07-12).
#
# Copy to `.env` on the Pi (chmod 600) and fill in. `.env` is gitignored —
# secrets never enter the repo, logs, or chat (ATLAS-API-008).
#
#   cp env.example .env && chmod 600 .env

# TaoStats API key (Phase 4) — from the TaoStats dashboard.
# Base URL https://api.taostats.io, sent as `Authorization: <key>` header.
# DESIGN TARGET: the FREE tier — 5/min, 10,000/month (corrected from
# "day" at the Phase 4 discovery gate, 2026-07-12). All rate/quota
# controls (ATLAS-API/LIVE) are built around free-tier limits so the
# system stays correct if the key is ever downgraded; a paid key
# simply has headroom. Atlas self-caps at 2/min — never fills 5/min.
TAOSTATS_API_KEY=

# TaoSwap (https://api.taoswap.org) is keyless — no variable needed.
# CoinGecko simple/price (TAO/USD cross-check) is keyless — no variable needed.

# --- Telegram (Phase 5) ---
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN is normally written by `hermes gateway setup` into the
# Pi's ~/.hermes/.env; the outbound notifier reuses that file (see
# telegram/config.json credential_env_files) — do NOT duplicate it here. Set
# it here only if you are not using the Hermes wizard.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
#
# TELEGRAM_ALERT_CHAT_ID — the ONE value the operator supplies: your numeric
# Telegram id (from @userinfobot), the destination for outbound alerts.
# Message @userinfobot, then put the number here (or in ~/.hermes/.env).
TELEGRAM_ALERT_CHAT_ID=
